From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:16:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/48] wayland: tell sandboxed clients apart with
 security-context-v1

Implement wp_security_context_manager_v1 so sandbox engines such as
Flatpak can open a listening socket for their apps and attach the
engine, app ID and instance ID to every connection made through it.

Every client is sorted when it connects. Connections through a security
context are sandboxed. Any other connection counts as unsandboxed only
when the process that connected, pinned by a pidfd taken from the
socket, still runs and shares the compositor's root mount, which no
process inside a mount namespace of its own does. Clients that cannot be
verified, because the process already exited or its mounts cannot be
read, count as sandboxed.

Only unsandboxed clients see the manager, so sandboxed apps can neither
nest security contexts nor claim another app's ID. Protocols that should
stay out of sandboxes filter their globals with
meta_wayland_filter_unsandboxed().
